der": 18, "widgets_values_named": {"codec": "auto", "filename_prefix": "video/MiniMax_H3", "format": "auto", "format.codec": "auto"}}, {"mode": 0, "outputs": [{"name": "positive", "links": [236], "label": "positive", "type": "CONDITIONING", "localized_name": "positive"}, {"name": "LATENT", "links": [234], "label": "LATENT", "type": "LATENT", "localized_name": "LATENT"}], "size": [435.6689758300781, 437.2620544433594], "pos": [-1348.3152304968035, 4753.184407832022], "widgets_values": ["integrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] A product-grade extreme macro shot, commercial advertising quality, ultra-high-definition 4K, digitally clean with zero grain, zero noise and zero compression artifacts, high micro-contrast, true-to-life color and tack-sharp edges from corner to corner. A single clear water droplet rests on the surface of a fresh green leaf, filling the centre of the frame; the leaf's cell structure, fine veins and the tiny hairs along its edge are all crisply resolved, and the droplet itself holds a sharp inverted reflection of a bright window and a sliver of blue sky. Raking low sunlight from the upper left grazes across the leaf, so every ridge of the surface casts a clean shadow. From 00:00.00 to 00:02.00 the droplet trembles slightly and begins to slide a few millimetres down the leaf toward the tip. The camera glides sideways at a slow, steady speed, keeping the droplet centred and staying perfectly parallel to the leaf surface.\nAt 00:02.00 the droplet meets a smaller bead and merges into one larger bead in a single clean snap, with a brief sharp specular highlight running around its rim.\nFrom 00:03.00 to 00:06.00 the larger bead rolls on toward the leaf tip, deforming slightly as it moves, its surface reflecting the leaf's green underside and the bright sky above. The camera keeps tracking sideways with it at matched speed, focus locked, the background dissolving into a smooth clean green blur with no banding.\nAt 00:06.00 the bead reaches the tip, 